The payload is 256 KiB whose byte differences at distance 4 compress well,
so that the archive stays small, generated by this small python program:

open('delta_payload.bin', 'wb').write(
    bytes((i * i + (i >> 8)) & 0xff for i in range(256 * 1024)))

Being several times larger than the reader's 64 KiB uncompressed buffer, it
covers the Delta history being carried across calls to decompress().

The archive was then created with 7-Zip 26.03:

7zz a -m0=Delta:4 -m1=Deflate -mhc=off -mtm=off test_read_format_7zip_deflate_delta.7z delta_payload.bin -y

begin 664 test_read_format_7zip_deflate_delta.7z.uu
